WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.743
NOT IN looks like a simple anti-membership test But
if the inner set

00:00:05.769 --> 00:00:13.023
contains NULL PostgreSQL cannot prove that an outer
value differs from the unknown value The

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:18.737
condition can become UNKNOWN rather than TRUE
Because WHERE keeps only TRUE

00:00:18.974 --> 00:00:24.536
rows you expected may disappear This is one of the
most important edge

00:00:24.549 --> 00:00:25.957
cases in this module
